            <ArticleTitle>Limbus Vertebra on Bone Scintigraphy in a Pediatric Patient.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>915-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1097/RLU.0000000000000970</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Limbus vertebra involving the anterosuperior corner of a vertebral body is usually seen in adult patients, and it generally does not cause symptoms. An 8-year-old girl experienced lower back pain. Bone SPECT images revealed significantly increased tracer activity in the region of the anterior L4 vertebral body, which was shown on MRI to be a limbus vertebra.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
